<!-- A batch of a session that negotiated compression: the one-byte batch
     header, then the batch's payload, to the end of the unit.

     Upstream writes the header into the batch buffer right after the stream
     length (`io/zenoh-transport/src/common/batch.rs` @
     `let _ = writer.write_u8(h.as_u8());`), with the one flag of
     `io/zenoh-transport/src/common/batch.rs` @ `const COMPRESSION: u8 = 1; // 1 << 0`:

       bit 0    : compression  the payload is an LZ4 block
       bit 1..7 : reserved

     and clears the flag when the compressed form is not smaller, so the
     payload is then the batch's transport messages as they are. What the
     payload holds under the flag is an LZ4 block, a transform and not a
     layout; it is undone by the reader (`compression.rs` in
     wz-session-core), and the messages it gives back are read by their own
     documents.

     The header is counted inside the batch, whose size is upstream's
     `BatchSize`, a u16, so no payload reaches the bound stated here. -->
<scxml xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/07/scxml"
       xmlns:sce="http://sce.dev/ext"
       sce:kind="codec" sce:default-endian="little" name="compressed_batch">
  <datamodel>
    <sce:flags id="header" sce:type="uint8" sce:byte="0" sce:bit-size="8">
      <sce:flag name="compression" bit="0"/>
    </sce:flags>
    <sce:field id="payload" sce:type="bytes" sce:byte="1" sce:bit-size="tail"
               sce:max-size="65535"/>
  </datamodel>
</scxml>
